# Backend Development Rules

## When to Check These Rules
- When working on models or controllers
- When writing database queries or migrations
- When implementing background jobs
- When creating or modifying API endpoints
- When handling data processing or business logic

## Code Style
- Follow RuboCop Rails conventions
- Use named parameters over positional parameters
- Keep methods small and focused
- Use proper naming conventions
- Document complex methods

## Class Definitions
- Use semicolons to join class namespaces together (e.g., `class Marketing::BuyflowUrlBuilder` instead of `module Marketing; class BuyflowUrlBuilder`)
- This makes the namespace hierarchy clearer and more concise
- Example:
  ```ruby
  # Good
  class Marketing::BuyflowUrlBuilder
    # ...
  end

  # Bad
  module Marketing
    class BuyflowUrlBuilder
      # ...
    end
  end
  ```

## Common Mistakes to Avoid
- Using positional parameters instead of named parameters
- Creating N+1 queries
- Not using eager loading when needed
- Mixing business logic in controllers
- Not handling errors properly
- Using ActiveJob instead of Sidekiq
- Not implementing proper validation
- Not using appropriate caching strategies
- Not following RESTful conventions
- Not documenting complex methods

## Database Optimization
- Use includes for eager loading
- Avoid N+1 queries
- Follow ActiveRecord best practices
- Use appropriate indexes
- Optimize complex queries
- Use counter caches when needed

## Background Jobs
- Use Sidekiq exclusively
- Location: app/sidekiq
- Never use ActiveJob or app/jobs
- Follow Sidekiq best practices
- Implement proper error handling
- Use appropriate retry strategies

## API Development
- Follow RESTful conventions
- Use proper HTTP methods
- Implement proper error responses
- Use versioning when needed
- Document API endpoints
- Handle authentication properly

## Data Processing
- Keep business logic in models
- Use service objects for complex operations
- Implement proper validation
- Use appropriate caching
- Handle edge cases
- Log important operations

## Examples

✅ Correct:
```ruby
# Using named parameters
def create_user(name:, email:, role: :user)
  # ...
end

# Proper eager loading
User.includes(:posts).where(active: true)

# Sidekiq job
class ProcessUserJob
  include Sidekiq::Job
  
  def perform(user_id)
    # ...
  end
end
```

❌ Incorrect:
- Positional parameters
- N+1 queries
- Business logic in controllers
- ActiveJob usage
- Poor error handling

## Validation Checklist
- [ ] Code follows RuboCop conventions
- [ ] Database queries are optimized
- [ ] Background jobs use Sidekiq
- [ ] Error handling is implemented
- [ ] Business logic is properly separated
- [ ] API endpoints are properly documented
